&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notre équipe data Customer Relationship recherche un·e Data manager basé·e à Paris.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre vision de la Pricing Excellence repose sur une approche globale de Revenue Growth Management (RGM) visant à établir le juste prix pour le consommateur et ainsi maximiser la valeur client et la rentabilité de l&#39;entreprise. Notre objectif est de délivrer une tarification data-driven qui équilibre le coût total, la perception client et la viabilité financière de l&#39;entreprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pour cela, nous exploitons les outils digitaux, la Data et l&#39;Intelligence Artificielle afin de maximiser les revenus et d&#39;assurer une efficacité opérationnelle orientée vers le client. L&#39;équipe est structurée autour d&#39;un Centre d&#39;Excellence Pricing et d&#39;une équipe Data &amp;amp; AI, qui développent de concert des solutions novatrices et industrielles pour optimiser proactivement la tarification et l&#39;expérience client.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION ET IMPACT STRATÉGIQUE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que &lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; AI Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, tu rejoins l&#39;équipe de direction Digital Customer Relationship au sein de laquelle tu seras garant de la définition des priorités DATA (gouvernance, Business Intelligence, modèle de données, référentiels, IA) pour l&#39;activité &lt;strong&gt;Pricing&lt;/strong&gt;. Tu définiras et porteras la vision stratégique Data &amp;amp; AI qui permet d’accompagner la transformation du Pricing et du RGM à l’échelle de l’entreprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Membre clé du leadership, tu pilotes une organisation d&#39;une dizaine d&#39;experts Data (Data Scientists, Data Engineers, Analytics Engineers) et tu garantis l’alignement parfait entre l&#39;innovation technologique, l&#39;excellence opérationnelle et les ambitions économiques globales du groupe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSABILITÉS CLÉS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vision stratégique &amp;amp; feuille de route Data:&lt;/strong&gt; définir la trajectoire Data &amp;amp; AI pluriannuelle (gouvernance, IA générative &amp;amp; prédictive, architecture, BI, référentiels) alignée sur les enjeux stratégiques du Pricing et du RGM. Arbitrer et prioriser les investissements technologiques à haut ROI en étroite collaboration avec les Product Managers et les représentants métier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership, culture &amp;amp; développement des talents:&lt;/strong&gt; inspirer, structurer et faire évoluer une équipe à fort niveau d&#39;expertise. Instaurer un environnement d&#39;excellence, attirer les meilleurs talents, développer le leadership des collaborateurs et garantir un modèle d&#39;organisation agile, bienveillant et performant.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gouvernance, ROI &amp;amp; création de valeur Business:&lt;/strong&gt; incarner la culture de la valeur auprès des directions métiers (Revenue Management, Directeurs Commerciaux, Finance). Définir la grille d&#39;évaluation de la création de valeur apportée par les solutions IA et assurer une gouvernance rigoureuse des actifs Data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellence opérationnelle:&lt;/strong&gt; garantir l&#39;excellence technique et le niveau d&#39;exigence industriel (robustesse, sécurité, éthique de l&#39;IA, monitoring, haute disponibilité). Insuffler la culture MLOps/DataOps pour accélérer le passage de l&#39;expérimentation à la production à grande échelle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence transversale:&lt;/strong&gt; garantir un alignement fluide avec les Engineering Managers et les Product Managers, dans et en dehors du domaine digital. Inculquer une véritable culture de la Data au sein des équipes produits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gestion budgétaire &amp;amp; pilotage économique:&lt;/strong&gt; définir, piloter et gérer le budget global de l&#39;équipe et des infrastructures Data/IA associées. Assurer la planification financière annuelle et pluriannuelle (horizon 3 ans), en optimisant les coûts liés aux RUN (infrastructures cloud, coûts de calcul et licences) tout en maximisant la valeur produite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PROFIL RECHERCHÉ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience&lt;/strong&gt;: expérience confirmée dans la Data &amp;amp; l&#39;IA, dont au moins 4 à 5 ans sur des fonctions de management d&#39;équipes pluridisciplinaires ou au sein d&#39;une leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compétences stratégiques&lt;/strong&gt;: capacité démontrée à traduire des enjeux business complexes (Pricing, Retail, RGM) en stratégies Data &amp;amp; AI applicables et rentables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;: posture de leader inspirant, capacité à négocier et à influencer, excellence managériale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Savoir-faire technique&lt;/strong&gt;: solide culture de l&#39;industrialisation IA (DataOps/MLOps), de la gouvernance des données et de l&#39;architecture moderne des plateformes Data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Imaginez si la technologie nous permettait de repousser les frontières et d&#39;offrir des expériences sportives inédites. C&#39;est précisément notre ambition chez Decathlon Digital ! Nous sommes une équipe de plus de 5 000 experts en ingénierie logicielle, gestion de produits, données, cloud et cybersécurité, répartis à Paris, Lille et Amsterdam. Ensemble, nous créons la plus vaste plateforme sportive numérique, en exploitant les innovations technologiques pour optimiser la chaîne de valeur, concevoir des expériences connectées et donner une seconde vie à nos produits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changeons la donne pour de bon.&lt;/strong&gt; Notre passion du sport nous guide et nous voulons qu’elle perdure. C’est pourquoi nous nous engageons à bâtir un modèle technologique plus durable, en réduisant notre impact direct sur l&#39;environnement, et en créant un espace sûr et inclusif pour apprendre et nous épanouir ensemble. Rejoins l’équipe et façonnons le futur du sport.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4PS is part of the Hilti Group&lt;/strong&gt;, which gives our people access to international opportunities and development programs within the wider Hilti organization. This vacancy is part of Hilti’s Global Trainee Program. Interested in joining the program? Please submit your application directly via &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.hilti.group/de-ch/stellenangebote/19051-en/global-trainee-program-outperformer-software-business-track-m-f-x/&quot;&gt;Hilti Careerpage&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Construction technology is being reinvented. Be part of it.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Construction is one of the world&#39;s largest industries, and one of its least digitized. That is changing fast. At Hilti, we are not only developing software products - we are building and growing digital businesses around them. Hilti is at the centre of that shift, with a growing portfolio of software products that connect jobsites, offices, teams, and tools across the entire construction lifecycle. We are looking for ambitious, internationally mobile early-career talents with a global mindset who are excited about technology but see their future in business and leadership rather than in a purely technical software career.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Software &amp;amp; Digital Business Track of Hilti&#39;s Outperformer Program is a two-year accelerated development program that prepares you for a commercial, international leadership career in our software and digital businesses. You will learn how technology becomes customer value, how software businesses grow, how products are brought to market, and how commercial decisions are made. This is not a rotation program where you shadow senior leaders. From day one, you carry real responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Software Track is designed to build the next generation of software business leaders at Hilti – Business Owners, Business Directors, Segment Managers and ultimately Senior Management Team members. If you want a structured path to running a business, this program is built for that outcome.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The program places you inside one of two business units:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Construction Software: Home to Fieldwire (Field Software for project and workforce management), ON!Track (asset management), and 4PS (construction business management). You will work directly with customers, product teams, and business leadership across Europe and beyond.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fastening &amp;amp; Protection Solutions: Where design &amp;amp; engineering software for structural connections (e.g. PROFIS Engineering Suite), MEP supports and passive fire protection systems are developed and brought to market across a global customer base of structural and mechanical engineers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For the Construction Software business unit, the program is structured to provide a balanced foundation in customer and market exposure, software product understanding, and business experience, while giving you the opportunity to work with at least two software products during the program:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​Year 1: Begin with a 12-month sales assignment, developing direct customer insight and understanding the business challenges addressed by our software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​Year 2: Undertake three rotations of 3–6 months each across product and business teams, including exposure to an international project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​For the Fastening &amp;amp; Protection Solution business unit, the program provides exposure to product management , software development, exposure to customers and start-ups and international project experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​Year 1: Begin with a 12-month product management assignment, building product understanding and market insight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​Year 2: Undertake three rotations of 3–6 months each, involving international projects that broaden your business perspective and global exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have a dedicated senior mentor from the start, direct exposure to executive leadership, and a peer cohort of Global Trainees across all Hilti business tracks globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are close to graduating or have recently completed a Master&#39;s degree - your degree is likely to be in construction management, civil engineering, or mechanical engineering with a focus on construction, Computer Science, or also Business study programs with an affinity for Software and construction. What matters more than your degree subject is the combination of traits below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global mobility - you are willing and able to relocate internationally, multiple times. A global thinker who is keen for diverse cultural experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital and AI orientation - you think natively in digital workflows, comfortable with software tools, and know the power and potential of AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language - you are fluent in English and/or German, Dutch, French, Spanish or Italian. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial instinct - you are drawn to how businesses grow, how customers make decisions, and how products create.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low ego, high drive - you take the work seriously and yourself lightly. You seek feedback, move fast, and are energised by ambiguity rather than unsettled by it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are at the start of your career and have maximum three years of junior work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What’s In It for You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​​Show us what you can do, and in return, we promise you the experience of a lifetime. We offer you a transformative journey filled with learning, growth, and invaluable experiences that will shape your perspective and personal and professional development. On top of that, you’ll also take part in some fascinating courses and events:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introductory Global Summit: Experience 4 days at our global headquarters in Liechtenstein, featuring the presence of our Executive Board and Global Senior Leadership. The summit offers a comprehensive overview of our business, while fostering soft skill development and meaningful collaboration with fellow program participants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social Project Summit: 7 days dedicated to building a better future, with contribution to a hands-on, high-impact community project. This experience offers the chance to immerse yourself in a different culture while actively improving living conditions for those in need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership Summit: An enriching learning journey in partnership with a renowned business school, featuring online modules and collaborative projects with fellow program participants. The experience concludes with a 5-day on-campus summit to deepen insights and to foster business and leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Hilti&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hilti is a global leader in construction innovation, with more than 34,000 team members across 120 countries. Guided by our purpose, Making Construction Better, we’re driven to keep learning, growing, and finding new ways to make a lasting impact. Here, you’ll be empowered to use your strengths, work with a global and inclusive team, and take on meaningful challenges. At Hilti, you’ll have the chance to make your ideas, achievements, and growth real through purpose, passion, and teamwork.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about our recruitment process: https://careers.hilti.group/en/candidate-interview-preparation/&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Commitment to Inclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​​At Hilti, inclusion is a key focus in how we work, lead, and grow together. We are committed to embracing diversity of thought and creating an environment that is inclusive of everyone, everywhere. We continuously strive to ensure every voice is valued and every team member feels empowered to contribute. By building on this foundation, we strengthen our teams, our innovation, and our impact, making construction better together.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​Exciting software journey: You will dive into the fast-paced world of our construction software business, gaining exposure to innovative digital solutions that are transforming one of the world&#39;s largest industries.&lt;br&gt;​&lt;br&gt;​Global cross-team collaboration: You will work with colleagues worldwide and get guidance from a dedicated mentor as you grow in your career.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​We hire for a career, not for a position. If you are looking for long-term career prospects and opportunities to grow, this is the perfect start.​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​Are you ready to jumpstart your career? Our hiring process is designed to help you showcase your skills and experience. The process has multiple steps and requires a longer period of time:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It all starts with your application and a video interview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get connected with our HR team in an online interview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get ready to flex your problem-solving muscles with our online Business Case Round.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impress our Business Line Managers with your presentation skills and insights during the next round.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And, if you make it to the end, you&#39;ll receive an invitation to our Assessment Center.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​Exciting, right? Let&#39;s get started!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4PS is part of the Hilti Group&lt;/strong&gt;, which gives our people access to international opportunities and development programs within the wider Hilti organization. This vacancy is part of Hilti’s Global Trainee Program. Interested in joining the program? Please submit your application directly via &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.hilti.group/de-ch/stellenangebote/19051-en/global-trainee-program-outperformer-software-business-track-m-f-x/&quot;&gt;Hilti Careerpage&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​The Assessment Center will take place in Liechtenstein at Hilti Headquarter on December 1st and 2nd, 2026. Applications will be reviewed in the order they’re received, so we encourage you to apply as soon as possible since there are limited spots for the Assessment Center!​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about our recruitment process:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.hilti.group/en/candidate-interview-preparation/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Candidate Interview Preparation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​​For further questions, please feel free to contact Vanessa Furtner ----- and (My LinkedIn).&lt;br&gt;​&lt;br&gt;*For non-EU / EFTA citizens: Please state your eligibility status to work in EU or UK countries and note that if you do not own a valid work permit, Hilti cannot guarantee your final employment due to authority regulations.​&lt;/p&gt;
