&lt;p&gt;Product Manager&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; UK (remote)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reachdesk is the first truly end-to-end global SaaS gifting and swag platform, helping B2B companies create meaningful connections with prospects, customers, and employees, while driving measurable ROI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe gifting is more than just a transaction: it’s about building genuine human connections that fuel business growth. Whether it’s engaging prospects, celebrating customers, or recognizing employees, our platform makes it easy to deliver personalized gifts, branded swag, and unforgettable event &amp;amp; brand experiences at scale through automated sourcing, storage, and global delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trusted by many of the most recognized names in technology and SaaS, Reachdesk integrates effortlessly with marketing, sales, and HRIS tech stacks and is powered by our world-class team across New York, London, and Lisbon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re growing, and we’re currently looking for a Product Manager to join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager at Reachdesk, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the Reachdesk Platform. You will be accountable for turning complex customer and business problems into software products that deliver measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Chief Product Officer, you’ll lead product initiatives end-to-end,&amp;nbsp; from identifying and deeply understanding the right problems to solve, through discovery and delivery, to launch, adoption, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll operate with a high degree of autonomy, proactively building context across customers, the market, internal stakeholders, data, and technology to understand what Reachdesk needs to achieve its goals. You’ll also make sound decisions when the path forward isn’t obvious.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner closely with Engineering and Design and work across the wider business to create alignment, communicate decisions clearly, and ensure what we build is successfully launched, adopted, and delivers the outcomes we set out to achieve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy solving difficult problems, taking ownership, and moving comfortably between customer, technical, and business conversations, you’ll thrive in this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set product direction and priorities&lt;/strong&gt;, bringing together company goals, internal stakeholder needs, customer insight, market context, data, and technical considerations to focus on the highest-impact opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define problems and experiences before solutions&lt;/strong&gt;, creating clear stories, journeys, and shared context so the Design and Engineering teams understand the problem and intended outcomes before determining the solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead product initiatives end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;, from discovery and solution definition through delivery, rollout, and iteration, partnering with Engineering to manage scope, make pragmatic trade-offs, and deliver valuable solutions at pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make sound product decisions and trade-offs&lt;/strong&gt;, balancing customer and business needs, commercial impact, user experience, and technical considerations while aligning the wider business on compromises, priorities, and expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop product opportunities with external partners&lt;/strong&gt;, building relationships with technology partners to uncover mutual opportunities, shape integrations, align roadmaps, and navigate the product and commercial considerations required to bring them to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Orchestrate successful launches and adoption&lt;/strong&gt;, working across Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, Services, Logistics, Finance, Legal, and other teams to ensure the business is ready and customers realise value from what we build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communicate with clarity throughout&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring leadership and teams across Reachdesk understand product decisions, progress, risks, changes, and results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong track record of &lt;strong&gt;owning B2B SaaS products end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;, from identifying the right problems through delivery, adoption, and measurable customer and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a &lt;strong&gt;strong problem solver&lt;/strong&gt; who gets to the root of complex problems, brings structure to ambiguity, and uses evidence and judgement to determine the right path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You operate with &lt;strong&gt;independence and initiative&lt;/strong&gt;: you seek out the customers, stakeholders, data, and context you need rather than waiting for direction, while staying anchored to Reachdesk’s goals and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;strong business and commercial awareness&lt;/strong&gt; and are curious about how the wider company operates, allowing you to understand competing needs and make pragmatic decisions beyond the boundaries of Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re &lt;strong&gt;technically fluent enough to work effectively with Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, understand systems, integrations, and constraints, ask the right questions, and contribute meaningfully to solution and scope decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an &lt;strong&gt;exceptional communicator&lt;/strong&gt;, able to create clarity, influence decisions, surface difficult trade-offs, and adapt how you communicate across customers, engineers, leadership, and teams throughout the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable &lt;strong&gt;operating externally as well as internally&lt;/strong&gt;, building productive relationships with technology partners, uncovering shared opportunities, influencing without authority, and navigating product, technical, and commercial conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong sense of &lt;strong&gt;product and user experience&lt;/strong&gt;, caring about the coherence and quality of the complete experience rather than whether individual requirements or features have simply been delivered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary with generous stock options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension with employer contributions (NEST)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Affordable Private Medical Insurance, including mental health support and fast access to care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO that increases the longer you’re with us, plus extra flexibility for life’s unexpected moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuinely collaborative culture with innovative, fun, and ambitious people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reachdesk believes that a diverse team helps us achieve our mission faster, and so we welcome applicants from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Privacy Policy: We process personal information submitted as part of your application in accordance with the Reachdesk Candidate Privacy Notice. Please review Reachdesk’s Privacy Policy here: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.reachdesk.com/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;www.reachdesk.com/candidate-privacy-policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Airbnb Hotels team is a fun, fast-growing group leading Airbnb’s expansion into the hotel sector. Operating with an entrepreneurial spirit, this team combines the simplicity, product excellence, and guest-centered ethos that define Airbnb. This team’s mission is to deliver the smoothest, most intuitive hotel booking experience for guests, while helping independent, boutique hotels easily drive incremental bookings so they can focus on delivering the best hospitality. The ultimate aim is to help more people discover high-quality hotels, creating value for guests and our hotel partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Account Executive, you will be responsible for converting leads into net‑new supply to support new-market launches and at pace to hit quarterly goals. Working the full sales funnel, you will proactively turn cold leads into warm sales opportunities helping to build the Hotels category’s market presence in the process through collaboration with other teams. This includes partnering, strategizing, and running daily operations directly with independent, boutique hotels , and ensuring that Airbnb sources&amp;nbsp; the best hotel inventory available to our guests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in Paris (hybrid, 2 days a week in the office).&amp;nbsp; It will start off as a 12-month FTC with the potential for conversion depending on individual performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet and exceed KPIs by owning the performance and success of assigned region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect new potential hotels through external research, networking, and use of Airbnb tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Securing new hotels involves targeted sales strategies and negotiating and closing the deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develops acquisition strategies and scalable, localised supply strategies for established and emerging markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertly position and communicate Airbnb’s value proposition to new partners via phone, email, and in-person&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add net new hotels by qualifying and moving leads through the funnel as quickly as possible, achieving defined quarterly goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find supply in and launch new markets: Own market launches including supporting lead generation and coordinating cross functionally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hotel onboarding as needed from won sales opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively promote and build strong relationships with hotels by demonstrating comprehensive knowledge of our platforms and confidently pitching their value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of professional experience, preferably in a fast growing startup tech or hospitality company working in sales and/or account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous hospitality experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in both English and French.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRM required; Proficiency in Salesforce, Gong and other scalable AI Sales prospecting tools is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to get things done with constantly changing priorities, projects and deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, organizational, and analytical skills, detail-oriented but moves fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to establish strong relationships with and influence partners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacity to balance day-to-day responsibilities with longer-term strategic execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a quick learner and you’re fearless about doing whatever it takes to get the job done, even if it means making mistakes along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel up to 25-30% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for Airbnb and travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We’ll Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for variable incentive pay, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The On-Target Earnings (“OTE”) range for this role is €98,000 to €115,000 gross per year, which includes a split of 80% (base pay) / 20% (variable incentive).&amp;nbsp;Of this OTE amount, the annual gross base salary range is €78,400 to €92,000.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The OTE reflected on this job posting is the target cash compensation a candidate could earn in a year if they achieve 100% of their performance or sales goals. The variable incentive is not guaranteed and is governed by the terms of Airbnb’s Hotels Variable Compensation Plan (the “Plan”). The actual payouts depend on performance against targets set under the “Plan” and may be higher or lower than the range listed on this job posting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The community you will join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is looking for a Marketing &amp;amp; CRM intern to join the Experiences team in Paris for a 6-month internship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with the person in charge of Demand for Paris Experiences, alongside Marketing, Growth and Product Management partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experiences let guests step into the real life of a destination: cook with a local chef, explore a hidden neighborhood with a historian, discover Paris through the eyes of the people who live there. Paris is one of our most iconic and competitive markets, and our job on the Demand side is to make sure the right guests find the right Experience at the right moment, whether they are visiting Paris or live nearby.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a curious, organized and data-friendly student who loves the craft of CRM and Operational Marketing: a sharp brief, a well-built email, a smart audience, and an analysis that tells us what to do next. You are comfortable juggling several campaigns at once, working with different teams, and turning numbers into clear recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The difference you will make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will support the Paris Experiences Demand lead on the day-to-day CRM and marketing activity that drives bookings. You will see a campaign from the first brief to the final analysis, and you will own your own projects along the way. During your internship, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Run email campaigns end to end&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write briefs for email campaigns (audience, objective, key messages, timing) and coordinate with copy, design and CRM partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute campaigns through our internal tools and planning process, including setup, QA and send follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze results after each send (opens, clicks, bookings, incrementality) and share clear learnings and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Support listing promotion and audience targeting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze cohorts of guests (new vs. returning, local vs. traveler, International vs Domestic) to understand behavior over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build simple, readable dashboards and recurring reports to select and prioritize listings based on quality, availability, performance and fit with the campaign&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Market and Supply teams to make sure what we promote is bookable and best-in-class&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn insights into concrete recommendations for audiences, timing and messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Follow local activations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational support and follow-up on field campaigns such as flyering, partnerships, events or more: briefing, logistics, timing, partners and results tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help measure what works locally and recommend future iterations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The intern experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern, you will be part of a team where you contribute to real projects with real business impact. Your manager, your team and our wider employee community will strive to be superhosts to you during your internship. We provide the support, mentorship and hands-on experience you need to learn quickly and make an impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get a front-row seat on how a global marketplace builds demand for a destination, with real ownership from day one: your campaigns go live and your analyses shape decisions. You’ll do it alongside a team that cares about craft, curiosity and human connection. You can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Marketing, Market Management and Acquisition partners to deliver projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present your analyses and recommendations to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek and give feedback throughout the internship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in the Experiences and broader Airbnb community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current student or recent graduate&lt;/strong&gt; (degree completed within the last 12 months) from a leading business school, engineering school or equivalent program in France, looking for a 6-month internship starting in January 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in French and English&lt;/strong&gt;, with excellent written communication: you can write a clear brief and a clear recap. You also have an eye for great copy and for what makes a message feel human&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A strong interest in marketing, CRM or growth&lt;/strong&gt;, and in travel, hospitality or community-driven products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious about data and performance metrics&lt;/strong&gt;, with an interest in using insights and quantitative analysis to evaluate campaigns, track performance, and inform decision-making. Experience with Claude or other AI tools to work faster and smarter is a must-have.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly organized and detail-oriented&lt;/strong&gt;, able to manage several campaigns and deadlines in parallel, and to follow up until everything is done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A collaborative mindset &lt;/strong&gt;and the confidence to work with people across teams, from Marketing to Product to Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have work authorization for France. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of this position, the successful applicant will need to be based in Paris, France to be able to conduct their work. Interns can expect to spend half of their time at the office and half working remotely with exact dates as agreed upon by the hiring manager. Additional in-person attendance for team meetings or offsites may be required as needed. Please note we are unable to provide relocation or visa sponsorship for this position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our commitment to inclusion &amp;amp; belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future.&amp;nbsp; This role may also be eligible for benefits and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;France Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€25.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€25.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
