<p><b>Om arbeidsgiveren:</b></p><p>Vår visjon er å skape en ledende spesialist av bemanningstjenester, og gjennom våre verdier skape gode løsninger og trygge vilkår i alle ledd. Våre verdier er: Trygghet, Engasjement, Nærhet og Kvalitet. Eterni har en unik kompetanse og erfaring med å levere gode og fleksible bemanningsløsninger til bransjer som er preget av sesongsvingninger og generell mangel på kvalifisert arbeidskraft. I tillegg til å tiltrekke oss lokal arbeidskraft, har Eterni god erfaring med rekruttering fra utlandet. Vi arbeider hver dag med å engasjere oss i hverandres arbeidsdag og virke, og ved tilstedeværelse skal vi være pådrivere for likestilling og et inkluderende arbeidsliv. Eterni tilbyr nyskapende, kompetente og bærekraftige løsninger for våre medarbeidere og kunder.</p>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Analytics Instrumentation is part of the Data Engineering and Monetization (DE&amp;amp;M) group, focused on the collection of Product Usage and Billing event data within GitLab. We build data collection platforms that enable product teams to assess user behavior and make evidence-based choices through privacy-conscious instrumentation that captures product usage throughout the user lifecycle.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Staff Backend Engineer, you’ll guide the design and development of a unified data infrastructure platform that consolidates analytics instrumentation across GitLab’s engineering organization. You’ll build and maintain backend systems that give the company visibility into customer usage patterns across GitLab SaaS and Self-Managed deployment environments. That data directly informs strategic product priorities and strategies. This role offers the opportunity to work on foundational infrastructure that simplifies instrumentation for teams at GitLab, replacing the complexity of multiple language-specific software development kits with a single, unified solution that teams can rely on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the design, implementation, and evolution of a unified data collection platform using Golang, Kubernetes, ClickHouse, and NATS, with success measured by reliability, performance, and adoption across GitLab teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the emission, transit, and quality of instrumentation data across the system, with success measured by data quality, data integrity, and usage billing accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance for usage billing and instrumentation systems during working hours, with success measured by timely incident handling, effective root cause analysis, and reliable service restoration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the organization with research and development teams and the enterprise data organization to deliver common solutions, with success measured by adoption across multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make technical choices that balance ease of use for product teams with reliability and correctness for data consumers, with success measured by platform usability and reliable downstream data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers through code reviews, design discussions, and clear technical documentation, with success measured by stronger code quality, faster technical alignment, and more maintainable systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience working with platform or infrastructure systems in production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in the Go programming language, with experience building and maintaining production services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong backend development experience, with the ability to design and deliver scalable, reliable systems serving internal and external customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience guiding technical design and making tradeoffs across system reliability, performance at scale, data quality, and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across team boundaries with product teams, data consumers, and other internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud native technologies and open source development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of mentoring other engineers and helping teams make clear, well-documented technical choices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Analytics Instrumentation team operates at the intersection of Product, Analytics, and customer-facing teams, providing data collection infrastructure that serves engineering teams across GitLab. We’re a distributed team of generalist engineers who tackle complex problems spanning the GitLab codebase, JavaScript, Go, and Python satellite services, data pipelines, and AI tool integration. We collaborate transparently across teams, deliver measurable results through efficient iteration, and build inclusive solutions that respect user privacy. Our work enables data-informed choices and planning across the organization. We’re involved in diverse projects from event data collection and privacy compliance tools to AI-powered analytics frameworks that help GitLab teams learn more about their users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW142035299 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW142035299 BCX0&quot;&gt;Resolve to Save Lives (RTSL)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; is a global health organization that partners locally and globally to create and scale solutions to the world’s deadliest &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;health threats. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Millions of people die from preventable health threats. We collaborate to close the gap between proven, life-saving solutions and the people who need them. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Since 2017, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;we’ve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; worked with governments and other partners in more than 60 countries to save millions of lives. We work toward a future where people live&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;longer, healthier lives, communities flourish, and economies thrive. This is an ambitious vision, and it inspires us and our partners to make progress every day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW70040856 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;Resolve to Save Lives (RTSL) works with governments and partners to strengthen and transform primary health care (PHC) to improve health and save lives. Our approach focuses on making PHC more prioritized, proactive and accountable for outcomes, and strengthening how care is organized, delivered, financed and measured. Drawing on expertise across RTSL&#39;s portfolio, we bring together solutions in health system resilience and epidemic readiness, digital health and data-driven decision-making, performance measurement and improvement, and sustainable health financing. We apply these capabilities to address priority health challenges, including cardiovascular health, maternal survival and sexual and reproductive health, while strengthening health systems to deliver more equitable, effective and resilient care. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW70040856 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;Position Purpose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director, Maternal &amp;amp; Reproductive Health will provide strategic and technical leadership for RTSL&#39;s portfolio to reduce preventable maternal deaths and improve sexual and reproductive health outcomes. The role will lead the development and implementation of a multi-country program that strengthens government capabilities to identify and address barriers to quality care, translate data into action, and deliver measurable improvements in health outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director will have overall accountability for the strategy, resources, quality, performance, and results of the maternal survival and reproductive health portfolio, leading a multidisciplinary team and working closely with governments, technical partners, and colleagues across RTSL to design, implement and scale evidence-informed approaches. The role requires deep expertise in sexual, reproductive and maternal health, strong program leadership, and the ability to translate technical evidence into practical, sustainable health system improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;100% Remote with travel as stated.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duration:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-time employment for a fixed term of 24 months.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW70040856 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;Core Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;and Portfolio Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the strategic direction, priorities and implementation approach for RTSL&#39;s maternal survival and reproductive health portfolio, exercising delegated authority to make program investment, resource allocation, and partnership decisions within approved organizational parameters and in alignment with country priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee a multi-country portfolio, with accountability for program planning, budget development and management, resource allocation, performance and delivery against strategic objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a multidisciplinary team, establishing clear responsibilities and performance expectations, overseeing staffing and talent development, addressing performance and capacity gaps, and building the capabilities needed for sustained program delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership and Program Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide expert technical leadership across maternal survival and sexual and reproductive health, including maternal death surveillance and response, quality maternal care, family planning, and adolescent pregnancy prevention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development and adaptation of evidence-informed approaches that connect data-driven learning with targeted improvements in clinical care, service delivery and wider health system capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the design and implementation of country programs, identifying opportunities to strengthen government leadership, institutional capabilities and sustainable approaches to improving health outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive innovation and collaboration across RTSL&#39;s technical teams, drawing on expertise in PHC delivery, digital health, measurement and financing to address priority health system bottlenecks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Engagement and Strategic Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead senior-level engagement with Ministries of Health and national partners to identify priorities, shape country strategies and secure government ownership of programs and results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage strategic partnerships with donors, multilateral agencies, technical institutions and implementing partners, identifying opportunities for collaboration, investment and program expansion, and representing RTSL in high-level technical and policy discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance, Learning and Accountability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain overall accountability for portfolio performance and results, establishing clear performance expectations and monitoring mechanisms, and using evidence and implementation learning to inform strategic decisions, address delivery challenges, and adapt approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the generation, synthesis and dissemination of evidence and practical learning to inform policy, program improvement and scale-up across countries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in medicine, public health, sexual and reproductive health, obstetrics and gynecology, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 15 years of relevant global health experience, including substantial technical and leadership experience in sexual, reproductive and maternal health in low- and middle-income countries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience developing and leading complex, multi-country programs, including strategic planning, budget oversight and accountability for results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience engaging senior government officials, donors and international partners, with the ability to build relationships and influence strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Abilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognized technical expertise in maternal survival and reproductive health, with a strong understanding of evidence-based interventions, health service delivery and health system strengthening.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead and develop multidisciplinary teams and manage programs across different countries and organizational functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data-driven program improvement, implementation challenges and approaches to translating evidence into sustainable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent strategic thinking, judgement, communication and leadership skills, with the ability to navigate complex political and operational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English required; proficiency in French desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel internationally, approximately 30% during program start-up and up to 25% thereafter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Resolve to Save Lives prides itself on cultivating a supportive, connected remote team doing work that matters. We do everything possible to ensure our employees are connected and set up for success.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;The salary range&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;for applicants based in the US&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; is $150,000 to $170,000 annually. The exact offer will be determined by various factors, such as the candidate&#39;s skills and experience relative to the requirements of the role. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;For applicants based outside the US&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;, salaries are set according to national labor rates for the international NGO sector.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, Resolve to Save Lives provides a generous package of benefits, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Health insurance for you and your dependents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:450,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:75}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Contributions toward retirement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:450,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:75}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Paid annual leave and sick leave, in addition to public holidays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:450,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:75}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Two paid, week-long organization-wide breaks at mid-year and end-of-year&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:450,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:75}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Professional development and home office setup benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:450,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:75}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Up-to-date computer equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:450,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:75}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:450,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:75}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anticipated Application Deadline:&lt;/strong&gt; 27 November 2026 (&lt;em&gt;This position may close earlier if a high volume of applications is received before the stated deadline&lt;/em&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0&quot;&gt;RTSL believes its programs are strengthened when they are developed and supported by individuals with diverse life experiences whose understanding of social and cultural issues can help make our work and workforce more inclusive. We encourage applications from and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0&quot;&gt;provide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0&quot;&gt; equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, ancestry, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, marital status, organ donor status, or status as a veteran. Resolve to Save Lives &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0&quot;&gt;complies with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0&quot;&gt; all applicable US EEO laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW71186963 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The SMB New Business Account Executive role is a critical role in building GitLab’s customer-base and continued long-term growth. The SMB New Business Account Executive will focus exclusively on acquiring new customers and generating new logos by executing on an inbound/outbound sales playbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own a territory and book of prospect accounts (including free GitLab users, trials, engaged leads and cold prospects). You will navigate it by leveraging data, developing a deep understanding of the product, the market, customer challenges and business needs. You will strategically build relationships with your accounts and lead a consultative sales cycle by painting the vision of DevSecOps with GitLab and helping them achieve business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role for someone who is competitive, self-starter and hungry, who is excited by forming new motions, thrives in a hunter environment and is energized by building relationships and business cases from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive selling into free users and base prospects within the SMB segment by articulating the value of GitLab. Engaging with inbound prospect and proactively reaching out to prospects showing potential and key signals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, co-create and consistently iterate on the outbound / new logo playbook and strategy to win new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce and execute against new creative prospecting and campaign ideas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of and act as the CEO for the book of business in your territory:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document the buying criteria &amp;amp; process, next steps &amp;amp; owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive prospecting strategies to build and maintain a healthy pipeline of new business opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work and collaborate with our Partner ecosystem to drive new business and value for our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize business and industry knowledge to research accounts, identify key players, generate interest, create/identify compelling events, and develop accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full sales cycle from initial contact to close by involving technical audience, multiple stakeholders and decision-makers, and articulating GitLab’s value proposition to across various industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master MEDPICC and Command of the Message on all opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams including Sales Development, Solution Architecture and Digital Marketing to develop winning strategies in targeting accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to root cause analyses on wins/losses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate lessons learned to the team, including the marketing team, the technical team and product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feedback: Effectively communicate learnings, feedback and challenges to relevant teams (including Product Development, Sales, and Marketing) to drive continuous improvement, and be the voice of the prospect by contributing product ideas to our public issue tracker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to documenting improvements in our sales handbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market knowledge: Maintain a foundational understanding of technologies related to GitLab’s market focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training &amp;amp; Certifications: Acquire industry standard certifications to build up credibility as a technical expert&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieving monthly and quarterly new logo acquisition targets, for both new logo count and booked ARR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You share our values, and work in accordance with those values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter with a proven track record of resilience, motivation and results&lt;/li&gt;
